Z||000000||Dumba$$||10-30-2001||05:28 PM||||i recently got a 120 mph speedo from an 86 GT  my ? is  do you also need the gear that is in the tranny?   the reason i ask is it seems to be off!<BR>i do have bigger tires    215-60-15   so i feel that will make a litle diff.  but it just seems to be a little more off since i put the other speedo in.<BR>my reason for the hurry is the car i got it out of is going to be traded within the next few days  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>4.9 caddy engine for sale 30,000 miles complete with bubba joes mounts!!  $750||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-31-2001||01:30 AM||||I don't know if you need to adjust/replace anything if you're installing it in your '84, but if you're installing it in your '86 it's just a plug 'n play.  The only thing I can think of that would throw it off (and not by much) would be tire size.  Actually, the size of your tires isn't off by much, if any.  I think stock rear size was 215-60-15.  You might want to pull the speedo out and try to re seat it just to be certain that the connections are good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PaulJK||10-31-2001||06:40 AM||||If you have a manual trans., the check engine light will come on if you have no gear on the sending unit. Just loosen the 10mm bolt holding the sensor to the transaxle and lift out the sensor. If there is no gear on the end of the shaft, DO NOT PANIC. you can get these at the local dealer for less than $10. Note: they will ask what color you want - Pontiac lists 5 different colors, which differ by a tooth or 2. i don't think it will matter much. Be sure to disconnect/reconnect the battery to clear the check engine lite.||||reg||1
